    "evidence_text": "PI3K inhibitors thus have considerable potential as molecular cancer therapeutics.\n\nPI103 was extensively metabolized, but distributed rapidly to tissues and tumors.\n\nThe tissues were first incubated with [3H]inositol, which was incorporated into the phosphoinositides.\n\nThere was no evidence for the existence of inositol 1:2-cyclic phosphate.\n\nPTEN Regulates PI(3,4)P2 Signaling Downstream of Class I PI3K\n\nThe PI3K signaling pathway regulates cell growth and movement and is heavily mutated in cancer.\n\nClass I PI3Ks synthesize the lipid messenger PI(3,4,5)P3.\n\nHere we show that PTEN also functions as a PI(3,4)P2 3-phosphatase, both in vitro and in vivo.\n\nNuclear PTEN functions as an essential regulator of SRF-dependent transcription to control smooth muscle differentiation\n\nPhosphoinositide 3-kinase signalling--which way to target?\n\nHowever, PI3Ks also modulate vital processes such as metabolic control and nutrient uptake.\n\nAll previously described members hydrolyze water soluble inositol phosphates.\n\nWe designate this 5-phosphatase as type IV.",
